==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthBoundary  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuthBoundary.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets the model invent an unauthenticated Operation whose outcome is Accepted, which is exactly the auth-bypass case FR-001 and the AuthRequiredEverywhere pattern are meant to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets an Accepted DeleteTask operation exist without a matching DeletionLog row, violating the one-log-per-deletion contract required by FR-018 and FR-012.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_PermanentDeletion, FR_018_DeletionLog
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_PermanentDeletion: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLog: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets two distinct DeletionLog rows reference the same Operation, which models a log row being rewritten or duplicated — the exact behaviour the append-only contract on task_deletions forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets a DeletionLog record a deleter who is not the actor of the operation it corresponds to — i.e. the log misattributes the action to the wrong member.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_FlatPermissions  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_FlatPermissions.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets Alloy give two structurally identical authenticated operations different outcomes — an implicit role/permission distinction that the flat-peer spec (Q3 = A) forbids.
    expected to FAIL: PermissionCompleteness, FR_004_FlatPermissions, FR_014_NoPerMemberVisibility, FR_015_FilterAnd, FR_016_ClearFilters
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_FlatPermissions: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_NoPerMemberVisibility: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_FilterAnd: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_ClearFilters: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskEditRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskEditRule.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets an EditTask operation on a Done task succeed without simultaneously reopening it (no newStatus set), violating the closed-task PATCH rule in FR-011.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskEditRule: FAIL (expected)

